        <node concept="3HG_t4" id="4QEfSMD5wuo" role="8EhU4">
          <property role="3HG_t5" value="source: item 10-53 half-value thickness&#10;symbol(s): `d_(1//2)`&#10;application domain: generic&#10;name: HalfValueThickness (specializes Length)&#10;quantity dimension: L^1&#10;measurement unit(s): m&#10;tensor order: 0&#10;definition: thickness (ISO 80000-3) of the attenuating layer that reduces the quantity of interest of a unidirectional beam of infinitesimal width to half of its initial value&#10;remarks: For exponential attenuation, `d_(1/2) = ln(2)/μ`. The quantity of interest is often the air kerma or exposure." />
        </node>
      </node>
      <node concept="1_pRso" id="4QEfSMD5wup" role="3Z9vGx">
        <property role="1_pRss" value="ISO-80000-10 item 10-54 total linear stopping power, linear stopping power" />
        <property role="1_pRsu" value="true" />
